<h3 dir="ltr">How Do You Make a Small Luxury Apartment Feel Larger Than It Is?</h3>
<p dir="ltr">Sightlines matter more than square footage. Positioning furniture, joinery, and even lighting to draw the eye toward the longest line in a room — a window, a hallway, an open door, makes a space read as bigger than its dimensions on paper. Mirrors used with restraint, low-profile furniture, and consistent flooring between rooms all reinforce the same effect. Our completed <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/muswell-hill-residence-interior-design/">Muswell Hill Edwardian residence joinery</a> project illustrates how continuous millwork visually expands room boundaries. This is where <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/residential-interior-design-london/">residential interior design</a> expertise shows: knowing which tricks actually work, and which just look like tricks. If you are unfamiliar with the craftsmanship involved, read <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/what-is-bespoke-joinery-a-guide-for-london-homeowners/">what is bespoke joinery in our guide for London homeowners</a>.</p>

